let __v_405 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"air fryer\",\"air fryers\",\"airfryer\"]},\"An air fryer is a small oven that blows hot air fast: chips, roast veg and salmon in 10 to 15 minutes with a spoon of oil. Worth it for one or two people who hate heating a big oven; skip it for four, since a 4-litre basket is one tray. £50 to £80 is plenty.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"slow cooker\",\"slow cookers\"]},\"A slow cooker is worth it if you are out all day: load it before work and cheap cuts are tender by dinner. Skip it if you want anything crisp or fast. A £30 one cooks the same as a £100 one.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"pressure cooker\",\"instant pot\",\"pressure cookers\"]},\"A pressure cooker is worth it if you cook beans, stews or tough meat from scratch: a beef stew is 40 minutes instead of two hours, and dried beans are 25. Skip it for anything quick or crisp, and know that it is a big pan to store. A 6-litre one suits most kitchens.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"bread maker\",\"bread machine\",\"bread makers\"]},\"A bread maker is not worth it for most people: skip it unless you eat a loaf a day, since it takes three to four hours for a small loaf with a soft crust, and a £15 tin in a hot oven makes better bread. It earns its space only if you want the dough made overnight with no hands.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dishwasher\",\"dishwashers\"]},\"A dishwasher is worth it for three or more people: it uses less water than washing up by hand and saves about half an hour a day. Skip it if you live alone and cook little, since filling it takes a week. Check the noise (under 45dB) if the kitchen is also the living room, and a 45cm slimline model fits a small kitchen.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"heat pump dryer\",\"heat pump dryers\",\"heat pump tumble dryer\",\"heat pump tumble drier\",\"heat pump drier\",\"heat pump condensing dryer\"]},\"A heat pump dryer is worth it if you dry two or more loads a week: it uses about half the electricity of a vented one, roughly 25p a cycle against 60p, so 150 to 200 pounds more up front pays back in about two years. It runs cooler, so a load takes an hour longer, and the fluff filter and condenser want clearing often. Skip it if you dry rarely, if the room is cold, or if you have nowhere to empty the water.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"tumble dryer\",\"tumble dryers\"]},\"A tumble dryer is worth it if you have no outside space or a house full of laundry: a heat-pump dryer costs more (£350 up) but uses about half the electricity of a vented one. Skip it if you have a garden and an airer: it is the most expensive way to dry clothes.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"smart thermostat\",\"smart thermostats\",\"heating thermostat\",\"nest thermostat\",\"hive thermostat\",\"tado\",\"thermostatic radiator valve\",\"thermostatic radiator valves\",\"trv\",\"trvs\"]},\"A smart thermostat is worth it if the house is empty in the day: about £50 to £100 a year off a gas bill, so £150 to £250 fitted pays back in two to three years. Skip it if someone is home all day, or if the heating is already set to come on only when you are in: turning the flow temperature down and putting thermostatic valves on the radiators gets much of the saving for a fraction of the price.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"water filter jug\",\"water filter jugs\",\"filter jug\",\"brita\",\"water filter\"]},\"A water filter changes the taste and takes out the chlorine, and a plumbed-in one under the sink is the same job done once instead of every jug: neither softens hard water nor takes out much else. Worth it if your tap water tastes of chlorine and you drink it cold all day, at about £20 for the jug and £4 a month for cartridges. A jug of tap water left in the fridge overnight does most of the same for nothing, so try that first.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"humidifier\",\"humidifiers\"]},\"A humidifier is worth it in one dry room, usually a bedroom with the heating on and the windows shut, if you wake with a dry throat or nosebleeds, or have a cold. Skip it in a room that has damp on the walls or condensation on the glass, because adding moisture makes that worse, and clean it every week: a dirty humidifier sprays mould into the air. £30 to £60 for a cool-mist one.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mattress topper\",\"mattress toppers\",\"bed topper\"]},\"A mattress topper is worth it if the mattress is sound but too firm, or you want it softer: 5cm of memory foam or a wool topper costs £60 to £120 and changes the feel for a fraction of a new mattress. It will not fix a mattress that sags, is over about eight years old or gives you backache, and a topper on a bad mattress is £100 spent on the wrong thing.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"water softener\",\"water softeners\",\"water softening\"]},\"A water softener is worth it in a hard water area if scale is a daily nuisance: kettles, shower screens and the washing machine stop furring up, and the boiler keeps its efficiency. It is about £1,000 to £2,000 fitted plus £100 to £150 a year in salt, so it is a family and hard-water answer rather than a flat one. A filter jug does not soften water, and a magnetic or electronic conditioner does not take the calcium out.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"robot mower\",\"robot mowers\",\"robot lawn mower\",\"robotic mower\"]},\"A robot mower is worth it for a flat, open lawn with no narrow gaps: it cuts a little every day, so the grass stays tidy and there is no grass to collect. It costs £500 to £1,500 and most need a boundary wire laid round the edge. Skip it for a small lawn, a steep slope, or one full of bulbs and toys.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"video doorbell\",\"video doorbells\",\"ring doorbell\",\"doorbell camera\"]},\"A video doorbell is worth it if parcels go missing or you cannot hear the door from where you work: £50 to £120, and stored clips usually need a subscription of £2 to £4 a month unless you take a local-storage model. Wired is more reliable than battery. Point it at your own path and door rather than the pavement, and if you rent, ask before drilling.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fan heater\",\"fan heaters\",\"electric heater\",\"electric heaters\",\"oil filled radiator\",\"convector heater\",\"space heater\",\"halogen heater\"]},\"A fan heater is worth it for one room for twenty minutes, not for a whole evening or a whole house: cheap to buy at £20 to £40 and dear to run, since 2kW is about 60p an hour on current electricity prices. For a room you sit in, an oil-filled radiator is silent and holds the heat after it clicks off, and heating the person beats heating the room: a throw, a hot water bottle and warm socks are free after the first winter.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fan\",\"fans\",\"electric fan\",\"tower fan\",\"pedestal fan\",\"desk fan\",\"floor fan\",\"standing fan\",\"cooling fan\"]},\"A fan does not cool the air, it moves it, and moving air over your skin is enough to feel a few degrees cooler, so it is worth it for sleeping in a hot room: a tower or pedestal fan at £25 to £60 is much quieter than a cheap one, and it costs a penny or two an hour to run. Put it in the window at night to pull cool air in, and skip portable air conditioning unless the room is also humid, since that is the expensive way round.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"robot vacuum\",\"robot hoover\",\"robot vacuums\"]},\"A robot vacuum is worth it as a daily top-up on hard floors and one level, not as a deep clean: skip it if the floor has stairs, thick rugs or a trail of cables and toys, since it will not get them and you still empty it. Best value in a house with a pet that sheds.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dehumidifier\",\"dehumidifiers\"]},\"A dehumidifier is worth it in a flat that steams up and grows black mould on the window frames: a 10 to 12 litre one dries washing indoors and stops the mould, which costs more to fix than the machine. Skip it if the damp is a leak or a broken gutter, since that needs fixing at the source.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"coffee machine\",\"bean to cup\",\"coffee machines\"]},\"A coffee machine is worth it if you drink two coffees a day at home: a £150 bean-to-cup pays for itself in about three months against buying them out. Skip it if you have one coffee a day: a £30 filter machine with fresh ground coffee tastes better than a cheap pod machine, and the pods are the expensive part.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"stand mixer\",\"kitchenaid\",\"stand mixers\"]},\"A stand mixer is worth it if you bake most weeks: it creams butter and kneads dough for you and lasts decades. Skip it if you bake a few times a year: a £15 hand mixer does the same job and lives in a drawer.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"meal kit\",\"meal kits\",\"recipe box\",\"hello fresh\",\"gousto\"]},\"A meal kit is worth it for the decision taken away, not the food: about £5 a portion and no waste. Skip it if you already cook, since the same dinner is £1.50 a portion from a supermarket. Try two boxes and cancel.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"kindle\",\"e reader\",\"ereader\",\"e-reader\"]},\"A Kindle is worth it if you read in bed or travel: a Paperwhite is readable in the dark, holds hundreds of books and the battery lasts weeks. Skip it if you mostly read at home: library ebooks through Libby or BorrowBox are free on a phone, and paper is better for anything with maps or photos. Buy last year's model, not the newest.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"noise cancelling headphones\",\"noise cancelling headphone\",\"noise cancelling\"]},\"Noise cancelling headphones are worth it if you commute by train, plane or sit in a loud office: over-ear ones cut the engine noise that earbuds let through. About £70 to £120 is the sweet spot, and last year's model sounds the same as the new one for half the price. Skip them for a quiet room or for cycling, where hearing traffic matters.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"fitness tracker\",\"fitness trackers\",\"fitbit\"]},\"A fitness tracker is worth it for steps and sleep, not for the heart-rate number: a £25 band counts steps and sleep well, and a watch ten times the price adds mostly a screen and GPS. Skip it if you already walk enough and know it, since most people stop looking after a month.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"smart watch\",\"smart watches\",\"apple watch\"]},\"A smart watch is worth it if you want notifications, contactless payment and a run tracker on your wrist without getting your phone out. Skip it if you only want steps, where a £25 band does the same. An iPhone pairs best with an Apple Watch, an Android with a Wear OS watch or a Garmin.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"standing desk\",\"standing desks\",\"sit stand desk\"]},\"A standing desk is worth it if you sit for eight hours and your back aches, and the useful part is changing position rather than standing all day: a £25 riser on the desk you have does most of it. Skip the motorised ones unless you know you will raise them, and stand for 20 minutes at a time rather than the afternoon.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"weighted blanket\",\"weighted blankets\"]},\"A weighted blanket is worth it if the feeling of weight settles you: about 10% of your body weight is the usual guide, and it helps some people fall asleep and does nothing for others. Skip it for a toddler, or for anyone who could not push it off, and try one under a duvet before spending £60.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"steam cleaner\",\"steam cleaners\",\"steam mop\"]},\"A steam cleaner is worth it for hard floors, tiles and grout, and the bathroom: it lifts grease with no chemicals and the water is free after the machine. Skip it on laminate, unsealed wood and anywhere the moisture can get under the floor, and skip it for carpets, where a hire machine once a year is cheaper than owning one.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"a cleaner\",\"the cleaner\",\"my cleaner\",\"our cleaner\",\"cleaners worth\",\"cleaning lady\",\"cleaning service\",\"housekeeper\"]},\"A cleaner is worth it if two hours back at the weekend matter more than £15 to £20 an hour: two hours a fortnight covers a flat. Go through an agency with insurance, agree in writing what is included and be in the first time. Skip it while you are paying off a debt.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"food processor\",\"food processors\",\"kitchen machine\"]},\"A food processor is worth it if you chop a lot of onions or make pastry: it does in a minute what a knife takes ten. Skip it if you cook simply, since it is heavy to wash up for one job. A £40 one chops as well as a £200 one.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"air purifier\",\"air purifiers\"]},\"An air purifier is worth it in a bedroom if you have hay fever, a cat or a sealed window: a HEPA filter on low all night changes how you sleep. Skip it for damp, which needs a dehumidifier, and check the replacement filters are cheap before you buy.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"heated airer\",\"heated clothes airer\",\"heated drying rack\",\"heated clothes horse\"]},\"A heated airer is worth it if you dry clothes indoors in winter: about 6p an hour against 50p or more for a tumble dryer, and it does not shrink anything. Skip it if you have a garden and dry outside in summer, and buy the larger winged one so a full wash fits on it. A cover cuts the drying time by half.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"electric blanket\",\"electric blankets\",\"heated blanket\"]},\"An electric blanket is worth it for a cold bedroom: 20 minutes before bed costs pennies and beats heating the room all evening. Skip it if it would be on all night, since a hot water bottle does the same for nothing, and replace one over ten years old.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"microwave\",\"microwaves\"]},\"A microwave is worth it for reheating, porridge, scrambled eggs and defrosting, not for cooking a meal from scratch: skip it if you want to roast or bake, since an oven does that better. A basic 800W one is enough; pay more for a bigger turntable and easier controls, not for modes nobody uses.\"]}]}")?;
