let __v_406 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"gym membership\",\"gym memberships\",\"join a gym\",\"joining a gym\",\"gym worth\",\"should i go to the gym\",\"should i go to gym\",\"shall i go to the gym\",\"should i go back to the gym\",\"should i go to the gym again\",\"should i bother going to the gym\",\"should i bother with the gym\",\"should i bother with a gym\",\"should i start going to the gym\",\"is it worth going to the gym\",\"worth going to the gym\",\"any point going to the gym\",\"should i go to the gym or\"]},\"A gym is worth it if the door is within ten minutes of you and you will go twice a week: the walk decides it, not the equipment. Skip it if the nearest one is a drive away, and pay monthly rather than a year up front. A £20 leisure-centre one you use beats a £60 one you dread.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"heat pump dryer\",\"heat pump tumble dryer\",\"heat pump drier\",\"heat pump tumble drier\",\"heat pump dryers\",\"heat pump condensing dryer\"]},\"A heat pump dryer is worth it if you dry two or more loads a week: the cycle uses about half the electricity of a vented one, roughly 25p against 60p, so it pays back its extra 150 to 200 pounds in about two years. It runs cooler and slower, so a load takes two hours and more, and it needs the fluff filter and condenser cleared often. Skip it if you dry rarely or have nowhere for the waste water, and never buy one without a heat pump if the room is cold.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"heat pump\",\"heat pumps\"]},\"A heat pump is worth it if you are replacing the boiler anyway and the house is insulated: the grant covers a few thousand, the running cost is close to gas, and it heats a well-insulated home steadily rather than in bursts. Skip it in a draughty house with no wall or loft insulation, since the insulation comes first and pays back faster.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"electric car\",\"electric cars\",\"ev \"]},\"An electric car is worth it if you can charge at home and do under about 200 miles a week: home charging is roughly 3p a mile against 15p for petrol, and there is almost no servicing. Skip it if you cannot charge at home, or if you regularly do long motorway runs, where public charging costs nearly as much as fuel.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"smart meter\",\"smart meters\"]},\"A smart meter is worth having: your supplier fits one free, and the in-home display shows what the kettle and the heating cost as you use them. Ask for a second-generation (SMETS2) one so it keeps working if you switch supplier. It will not cut the bill on its own.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"water meter\",\"water meters\"]},\"A water meter usually saves money if there are more bedrooms than people: the rule of thumb is that you pay less on a meter when there are fewer of you than rooms. Check the bill estimate first, and remember you can go back to an unmetered bill within the first year in England and Wales if it costs you more.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"season ticket\",\"season tickets\"]},\"A season ticket pays off at about three days a week: below that, the flexible or weekly options are usually cheaper. Work out the yearly cost against 40 weeks of daily returns before you commit, and check whether a part-time or flexi season covers the days you actually travel.\"]}]}")?;
frame.store("CHOICE_VALUE", __v_406.clone())?;
