let __v_701 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"down\",\"puffer\",\"padded\",\"padding\",\"quilted\",\"synthetic\",\"insulated\",\"insulation\"]},\"Down is the warmest for its weight and packs down small, so look for 600 fill power or more and it will last a decade, but it insulates badly once it is wet. Synthetic padding costs about half as much, is heavier and bulkier, and still keeps you warm when damp, which suits a wet winter better than down unless you want it for real cold.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"wedding\",\"funeral\",\"christening\",\"interview\",\"smart\",\"formal\",\"dress code\",\"party\",\"office\",\"town\",\"work\"]},\"For anything smart - a wedding, a funeral, a winter interview - a wool or wool-blend coat is the answer: it hangs properly over a dress or a suit, and a mid-calf length in navy, grey, camel or black goes with everything. Check that it closes over the jacket you will wear underneath and try it on in the shoes you will be standing in, because a heavy coat pushes the shoulders up.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"wool\",\"woollen\",\"woolen\",\"duffle\",\"tweed\",\"overcoat\"]},\"A wool coat is warm, smart enough for town and fine in a shower, but it gets heavy once it is soaked and wants dry cleaning rather than a wash. Check the lining and the buttons, buy it loose enough for a jumper under it, and keep it for the days you are not out in the rain.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"waterproof\",\"rain\",\"shell\",\"gore\",\"storm\",\"wet\"]},\"For rain, a waterproof shell with taped seams (Gore-Tex or similar) at £150 to £250 outlasts three cheap ones: check the hood, the zip and the seams under the arms, and try it on over a jumper. A shower-resistant jacket is fine for a dash to the shops and no good for a wet walk.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"worth\",\"expensive\",\"spend\",\"how much\",\"cheaper\",\"budget\",\"value\",\"price\"]},\"Yes, if it is one you will wear for years: a coat is the piece of clothing where the money shows, and £80 to £150 buys a padded coat that lasts a decade, £150 to £250 a waterproof shell that does not leak at the shoulders. Cheap coats cost more in the end because the zip goes and the seams soak through, so buy the best you can in a plain colour you will still wear in five years.\"]}]}")?;
