let __v_2898 = pyrt::literals::decode("{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"rice cooker\",\"rice cookers\"]},\"A rice cooker is worth it if rice is a daily thing: it times it, keeps it warm for an hour and leaves the hob free, and a 40 pound one cooks as well as a 200 pound one. Skip it if you eat rice twice a month, since a pan with a lid is the same rice in 12 minutes.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"soup maker\",\"soup makers\"]},\"A soup maker is worth it if you make soup most weeks and want one jug and no pan to watch: it cooks and blends in about 20 minutes. Skip it if you like soup with chunks in it, or cook for four, because most jugs hold 1.6 litres and the blade takes everything smooth.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"sous vide\",\"sous vide stick\",\"sous vide machine\",\"sous vide cooker\"]},\"Sous vide is worth it if you cook steak, chicken breast or eggs to a temperature and do not mind waiting: a 60 pound stick in a lidded pan holds the water steady for an hour or more, and nothing overcooks. Skip it if dinner has to be on the table in 20 minutes, where a thermometer and a hot pan get most of the way.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"dehydrator\",\"dehydrators\",\"food dehydrator\"]},\"A dehydrator is worth it if you dry things often: herbs, apple rings, jerky or vegetables for stock, in 4 to 12 hours at 40 to 60C with no oven on. Skip it if that is a twice-a-year job, since an oven on its lowest setting with the door ajar dries a tray at a time.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"juicer\",\"juicers\"]},\"A juicer is worth it only if you drink juice most mornings: it separates the pulp in seconds, and cleaning the mesh takes five minutes every time. Skip it if you would rather eat the fruit, which keeps the fibre the juice leaves behind.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"yogurt maker\",\"yoghurt maker\",\"yogurt makers\"]},\"A yogurt maker is worth it if you get through a tub a week: a litre of milk makes a litre of yogurt for about 60p, and it holds the warmth steady for 8 to 12 hours. Skip it if you eat yogurt now and then, since a flask and a warm cupboard do the same job.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"ice cream maker\",\"ice cream makers\"]},\"An ice cream maker is worth it if you make it more than a few times a summer: the bowl has to be frozen overnight, so it is never a last-minute thing, and a 40 pound one with a pre-frozen bowl is fine. Skip it if you would use it twice, where a loaf tin and a fork every half hour gets close.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"contact grill\",\"panini press\",\"sandwich press\",\"george foreman\",\"health grill\"]},\"A contact grill is worth it if you toast sandwiches or cook chops and vegetables for one or two: it heats both sides at once and the fat runs off. Skip it if you cook for four, since the plates take two sandwiches at a time, and skip it if you have a frying pan and a lid.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"electric steamer\",\"steam cooker\",\"food steamer\"]},\"An electric steamer is worth it if you steam vegetables, dumplings or fish often and like setting a timer and walking away: the tiers hold a whole dinner over one ring. Skip it if a pan with a colander and a lid already does it, which for most people it does.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"electric whisk\",\"hand whisk\",\"hand mixer\",\"electric hand whisk\"]},\"An electric hand whisk is worth it for anyone who creams butter or whips cream even a few times a month: about 15 pounds, a minute instead of ten with a fork, and it lives in a drawer. Skip it only if you bake twice a year.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"mandoline\",\"mandolines\",\"mandoline slicer\"]},\"A mandoline is worth it if you slice a lot of vegetables thin and even - gratins, slaw, pickles - and you will use the hand guard every single time. Skip it if you cook for one: a sharp knife is safer and nearly as quick.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"spiralizer\",\"spiralizers\",\"spiraliser\"]},\"A spiralizer is worth it only if you really eat courgette or carrot noodles: a 10 pound hand-held one does it in a minute and the counter-top ones add nothing. Skip it if you would use it once, where a julienne peeler does the same job and fits in a drawer.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"soda stream\",\"sodastream\",\"soda maker\",\"sparkling water maker\"]},\"A soda maker is worth it if you drink sparkling water every day: a gas cylinder makes about 60 litres for 10 pounds to swap, so it pays for itself in a few months and saves carrying bottles. Skip it if you drink it now and then, or would mostly use the flavour syrups, which cost more than supermarket bottles.\"]},{\"$tuple\":[{\"$tuple\":[\"vacuum sealer\",\"vacuum sealers\",\"food sealer\",\"food sealers\"]},\"A vacuum sealer is worth it if you buy meat in bulk or freeze portions: it stops freezer burn and the bags can be boiled, so a batch of chilli reheats in the bag. Skip it if you freeze little, since a freezer bag with the air pressed out does most of it.\"]}]}")?;
